WEBVTT

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.920
At the bottom of the ninth, this is a great chance for the Hornets to end the game.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.380
They've put a runner on second with a sacrifice bunt and two outs.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.240
And we're back to the top of the lineup.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:16.660
Play!

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:19.660
Strike!

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.980
Who would've thought Watts would give up a run.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.400
Two outs and a runner on second.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.630
If we don't get a run, we're going into extra innings.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.160
Safe! Safe!

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:43.490
What a comeback!

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:45.560
The closer gave up a run,

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.440
but Roy turned it around with his RBI!

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.720
That's the fourth consecutive win for the Hornets!

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:54.850
The Coyotes lost today, so the Hornets are only one game off the lead!

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.020
Hey, Junior.

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:58.000
Let's go.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:58.740
Yeah.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.080
You're here, Hornets.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:10.030
The division's finally starting to get interesting.

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:19.320
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:19.320
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:24.620
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:24.620
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:30.000
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:30.000
the only thing I truly have

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.290
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.290
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:40.630
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:40.630
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:45.890
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:45.890
the season of the coming summer began.

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:51.270
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:51.270
I had begun to understand many things

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:57.360
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:57.360
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:02.910
garakuta no yama kara

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:02.910
In the junk I've piled up,

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:06.990
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:06.990
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:12.290
hibike kono koe yo

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:12.290
Let my voice echo on.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:18.550
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:18.550
Let my heart resonate.

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:24.220
namida kareru made

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:24.220
Until my tears dry up,

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:29.270
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:29.270
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:34.600
namida hareru made

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:34.600
Until my tears clear away,

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:39.610
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:39.610
though I may lose my way,

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:43.450
egakikake no ima

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:43.450
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:44.950
kizamu

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:50.700
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:46.240
akashi

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:50.700
kono te de

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:56.530
The Creeping Shadow

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:56.530
The Creeping Shadow

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:00.450
These two teams are neck and neck in the Central Division of the Southern League.

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:03.370
Today's game has Texas Raiders against the Chicago Bisons.

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:08.790
The Raiders took the lead yesterday with Gibson Jr.'s home run.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:12.700
However, they're two runs behind at the top of the eighth,

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:14.850
and the Bisons haven't given them many chances.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.740
Ball! Ball four!

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:22.840
Now hitting, number 4:

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:26.260
Joe Gibson Jr.!

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:28.700
Yeah! It's Gibson!

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:30.690
Hit it big, Junior!

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:32.310
Umpire!

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:36.970
Oh? Bisons' manager, Johnson, is coming out.

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:38.780
He's making a pitching change.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:44.820
Attention, please. Pitcher, number 13:

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:48.580
Joe Gibson!

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:52.210
D-Dad?

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:55.850
He came back to the majors?

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.720
Now, with two outs and runners on first and second,

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.880
Joe Gibson steps on to the mound.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:05.550
His son, Gibson Jr., is at bat.

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:09.590
Who will win the first family showdown?

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:12.350
Gibson...

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:22.190
I'm impressed that you've managed to crawl your way back up.

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:26.620
I don't care whether you retire or not anymore.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:32.620
I'm just going to show you how much I've grown!

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:33.890
Play!

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:46.260
Strike!

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:50.080
92 mph?

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:53.100
He's back in the majors with that?

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:57.770
That's even slower than his pitches I saw in the minors.

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:02.280
Strike two!

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:04.950
I see.

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:10.120
You just brushed up on your control and breaking balls.

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:11.740
Ball.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:14.290
Ball.

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:22.340
However, with my heightened senses, I can even see the seams of the ball.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:26.440
I'm not the same as I was in my slump,

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:30.670
recklessly trying to make my bat hit the ball.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:35.430
Go back to the minors?

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:37.670
Sure, why not?

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:45.320
It takes suffering and frustration to become a top major leaguer.

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:54.290
I always respected you as a player,

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:58.330
and I could never respect you as a father,

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:04.210
but I will show you the utmost respect and gratitude, Dad.

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:07.800
WITH THIS BAT!

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:21.560
Strike out!

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:27.700
Gibson Jr. goes down without a swing!

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:35.950
At age 43, Gibson wins the family showdown with a 100 mph pitch!

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:38.920
Wow...

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:41.910
He's already throwing at 100!

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:46.130
Well, for that old man, it's not surprising.

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:50.520
Don't lower your guard, Junior.

00:06:54.150 --> 00:07:01.770
Now, I'd like to ask Mr. Gibson about defending the eighth inning and bringing the team to victory.

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:05.250
Today was your first father-son match.

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:07.680
How did you feel on the mound?

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:11.670
Being related doesn't mean much.

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:16.210
As Junior's one of the most fearsome batters in the majors,

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:18.040
I was actually nervous.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:27.130
I believe that I only won today because the baseball gods lent me their strength.

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:30.830
May I ask what your current goal is?

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:35.800
Well, it can't be anything other than getting to the World Series and winning it.

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:40.080
To that end, I'm going to use every ounce of strength I have.

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:43.100
The World Series...

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:48.540
The World Series, huh?

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:58.820
Now, regarding your trade request...

00:07:58.820 --> 00:08:04.080
You'd like to cancel it and remain on the Hornets, correct?

00:08:04.530 --> 00:08:05.650
Yeah.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:08.920
I feel like I could die with this team.

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:15.810
I want to see your team be number one, Papa.

00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:22.480
I want to see you be the best and smile on the field.

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:25.920
I'm gonna do it.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:29.810
After all, I'm in a good position to win the championships.

00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:30.660
True.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:32.920
The Hornets are amazing this year.

00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:35.570
But Watts is a little...

00:08:36.850 --> 00:08:40.240
Is something wrong with Watts?

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:45.420
It's the third and final game between the White Hawks and the Hornets.

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:47.670
This could become the Hornets' fifth consecutive win.

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:49.840
They're entering the top of the ninth with a one run lead.

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:52.880
The team has given the mound to their closer, Watts,

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:57.390
but he hasn't been doing well lately.

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:59.410
Will he be able to hold them down today?

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:06.700
Ball!

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:08.020
Ball four!

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:15.780
Now hitting, number 2: Costello!

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:23.700
That's too slow!

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:55.480
They won! The Coyotes won!

00:09:55.480 --> 00:10:00.900
This should rile them up for the start of their series against the Hornets tomorrow.

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:04.050
Damn, they won.

00:10:04.050 --> 00:10:05.950
This isn't good.

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:11.210
Now, we're only two games apart going into our final three-game series with the Coyotes.

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:15.900
But it's gonna be hard to fight for the top with Watts struggling.

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:19.670
He's failed twice as the closer.

00:10:19.670 --> 00:10:21.490
I wonder what happened.

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:23.140
He doesn't have the guts.

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:27.160
He'll be a free agent next year.

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:31.560
He's gonna sell himself to a stronger team for a lot of money.

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:35.630
He doesn't care about winning for the Hornets.

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:37.930
That's why he's not trying.

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:40.240
Hey, what do you think you're saying?

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:42.620
His own agent told me.

00:10:43.060 --> 00:10:47.510
He's having trouble with his hip, but he's still forcing himself to play.

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:48.250
What?

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:51.740
Are you serious?

00:10:51.740 --> 00:10:55.000
But... why would he do that?

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:57.170
That's how agents do their jobs.

00:10:57.620 --> 00:11:00.260
They can't sell injured players for much,

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:03.760
so they want to keep them playing even if it means the team will lose.

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:12.240
Basically, he's hiding his injury and playing, putting the team at risk.

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:14.610
Th-That can't be true!

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:16.610
It is.

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:18.650
Watts!

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:21.280
Guys, I'm sorry.

00:11:22.060 --> 00:11:25.670
I would have liked to defend today's game,

00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:27.610
but life isn't as easy as I thought.

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:31.490
I was just talking with the managers.

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:37.340
I asked them to disclose my injury and make me a relief pitcher starting tomorrow.

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:42.390
I left you in the dark and kept playing, but I can't burden you guys anymore.

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:44.890
Watts...

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:46.090
See ya.

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:50.780
What the hell?

00:11:50.780 --> 00:11:55.370
What was the point in continuing to play if he's just gonna disclose it?

00:11:55.370 --> 00:11:57.530
That's enough, Murdoch.

00:11:58.840 --> 00:12:01.140
Can't you tell how much he regrets it?

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:06.910
He's been with the Hornets his whole career, much longer than anyone else.

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:12.690
He also has the pride of being the closer for the past few years.

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:17.120
I don't know about his agent's plan,

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:22.630
but he probably forced himself to play because he wanted to help the Hornets until the end.

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:27.730
He doesn't care about winning because he'll transfer?

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:30.300
That's ridiculous!

00:12:30.300 --> 00:12:32.270
If it's going to be his last year on the Hornets,

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:35.890
he'd want to win the championship even more.

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:41.150
It's almost the deciding moment.

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:44.550
The final games for the top in the Central Division of the Northern League.

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:49.120
The Hornets are only two games behind the Coyotes.

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:52.020
The coaches have entrusted today's crucial game to Shigeno,

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:55.190
who's been playing magnificently in the second half of the season.

00:12:57.800 --> 00:12:59.070
Play ball!

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:00.630
Let's go, Shigeno!

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:03.340
I'll send you to hell if you lose this game!

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:09.390
I can't burden you guys anymore.

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:11.890
If Watts can't play,

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:14.520
then I'll make up for it!

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:17.900
Strike!

00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:21.320
Strike two!

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:24.810
Strike out!

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:31.150
All right, he's pitching well.

00:13:31.150 --> 00:13:32.120
Yeah.

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:34.830
Strike out!

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:44.130
Damn.

00:13:45.570 --> 00:13:47.300
Now hitting, number 5:

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:49.800
Silva!

00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:52.560
Damn, it's Silva.

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:56.480
I didn't want to face him with a runner.

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:01.700
Foul!

00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:06.390
His pitches are as fast as ever.

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:12.120
However, this is an important game that could decide the winner.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:19.010
I'll take down the Hornets with my bat today.

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:22.420
Ball.

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:24.490
Damn.

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:27.510
Man, why's he so damn persistent?

00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:31.850
Take this!

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:39.140
Out!

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:40.370
Damn!

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:53.750
We've had runners on every inning, but after seven innings we still don't have a run.

00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:57.870
Shigeno's pitching pretty well despite the incredible pressure of this game.

00:14:57.870 --> 00:15:03.260
Seeing his stability over the past few months, it's like he's our ace.

00:15:03.260 --> 00:15:04.150
Yeah.

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:15.810
All right!

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:25.860
Damn.

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:27.730
Let's go!

00:15:27.730 --> 00:15:29.200
An RBI!

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:30.530
Nice one, Keene!

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:31.990
Follow him, Parker!

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:36.460
Out!

00:15:37.720 --> 00:15:38.980
That was so close.

00:15:38.980 --> 00:15:40.910
Just a few more feet.

00:15:41.350 --> 00:15:42.640
Still,

00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:45.990
a one run lead is more than enough.

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:54.300
Now, I just have to defend our lead no matter what!

00:15:55.210 --> 00:15:56.810
Strike out!

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:58.030
Yeah!

00:16:01.340 --> 00:16:02.980
Strike out!

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:07.150
Strike out!

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:08.480
All right!

00:16:08.890 --> 00:16:11.060
Nice pitching, Shigeno!

00:16:19.190 --> 00:16:22.460
Man, those three didn't even try.

00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:26.560
It's the last inning, dear.

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:29.890
Yeah, if we hold the fort here, it's a step closer to victory.

00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:33.800
Is Shigeno pitching the entire game?

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:36.040
Show us something good, Shigeno!

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:39.640
Hey, is he still pitching?

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:42.030
Are you really sure, Boss?

00:16:42.030 --> 00:16:45.000
Even if Shigeno said he can keep pitching,

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:47.610
he's already past 130 pitches.

00:16:48.210 --> 00:16:52.730
Do you have another pitcher you can trust right now?

00:16:52.730 --> 00:16:54.070
Well...

00:16:54.590 --> 00:16:57.040
We can't lose this game no matter what.

00:16:57.040 --> 00:17:00.270
With his tenacity, he'll respond to that.

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:05.330
Just three more outs.

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:08.480
If we allow a hit, they'll get around to Silva.

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:10.290
Make sure you stay focused.

00:17:10.290 --> 00:17:12.090
Yeah, I know.

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:13.080
Play!

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:20.310
Out!

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:21.390
Damn.

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:23.680
Do whatever it takes to get me at bat.

00:17:31.080 --> 00:17:31.850
Ball!

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:43.710
Foul!

00:17:45.740 --> 00:17:47.140
He's doing it again.

00:17:47.140 --> 00:17:48.290
Time out!

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:53.210
What's this time out for?

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:55.380
Is something wrong with your left hand?

00:17:56.650 --> 00:18:01.470
You've been shaking it around and breathing into your fingers.

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:04.980
You don't usually do that.

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:08.460
I have?

00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:09.900
I didn't realize that.

00:18:11.870 --> 00:18:13.440
I see.

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:14.820
Then it's fine.

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:32.000
Ow!

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:37.800
All right.

00:18:39.290 --> 00:18:40.570
What the hell?

00:18:40.570 --> 00:18:43.720
What was that jolt of pain?

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:54.070
Too slow!

00:18:58.500 --> 00:18:59.280
Murdoch!

00:19:02.390 --> 00:19:03.140
Out!

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:03.990
Second base!

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:07.830
Lucky us!

00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:22.140
What is Shigeno doing?!

00:19:24.130 --> 00:19:25.440
Sorry.

00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:27.060
The ball just slipped out.

00:19:28.010 --> 00:19:30.090
Your pitches are slowing down.

00:19:30.090 --> 00:19:32.520
You need to focus more on your control.

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:35.530
In the worst case, we'll walk Silva.

00:19:35.530 --> 00:19:36.980
Yeah.

00:19:41.130 --> 00:19:43.820
Why does my hand feel so weird?

00:19:45.220 --> 00:19:46.990
Now hitting, number 5:

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:49.660
Silva!

00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:51.860
Please, Shigeno.

00:19:51.860 --> 00:19:53.080
Hold him down!

00:20:00.070 --> 00:20:01.590
Ball!

00:20:02.350 --> 00:20:04.550
What the heck was up with that pitch?

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:08.470
93 mph?

00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:11.390
Damn, he's getting tired here?

00:20:12.490 --> 00:20:13.810
Give me a break.

00:20:17.280 --> 00:20:18.570
Ball.

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:20.940
Ball.

00:20:20.940 --> 00:20:22.210
Ball three.

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:26.370
I came to hit your 100 miler!

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:29.310
I don't want some pathetic pitch.

00:20:30.010 --> 00:20:32.710
Man, what's going on?

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:35.790
Some sort of pain jolts my body right when I throw,

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:38.610
and each pitch makes it worse.

00:20:40.130 --> 00:20:41.790
Come on, Shigeno.

00:20:41.790 --> 00:20:43.330
Show me your 100 mph!

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:46.010
Damn it!

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:05.660
Out!

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:07.640
Game over!

00:21:07.640 --> 00:21:13.180
The Hornets take the first game of the three-game series!

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:26.510
H-Hello?

00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:28.980
Sorry for calling so early, Shigeno.

00:21:28.980 --> 00:21:31.180
Oh, it's fine.

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:35.560
I want to talk to you, so can you come to my office before practice?

00:21:38.010 --> 00:21:39.360
Hey, are you listening?

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:41.290
Oh, sure.

00:21:41.290 --> 00:21:42.770
Well, see you then.

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:46.280
Good.

00:21:46.790 --> 00:21:48.500
My hand feels just fine.

00:21:51.880 --> 00:21:53.330
I'm gonna be the closer?

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:55.010
Yeah.

00:21:55.010 --> 00:22:00.000
With Watts in his current condition, we need a replacement.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:04.670
You were the closer on the Bats and the Japanese national team.

00:22:05.210 --> 00:22:08.070
Your pitches are fast, and you get lots of strike outs.

00:22:08.070 --> 00:22:11.420
You're better suited to closing than you are to starting.

00:22:11.420 --> 00:22:16.990
Of course, we won't ask you to pitch today or tomorrow against the Coyotes

00:22:16.990 --> 00:22:19.040
when you just threw yesterday.

00:22:19.040 --> 00:22:23.690
I'd like you to start getting ready for our final six games next week.

00:22:24.490 --> 00:22:26.070
Well, can you do it?

00:22:28.990 --> 00:22:31.560
I'm ready whenever you need me.

00:22:31.560 --> 00:22:35.720
When you need me, I'll defend the team in Watts' place.

00:22:45.510 --> 00:22:51.010
kaze to hizashi no naka de

00:22:45.510 --> 00:22:51.010
Amid the wind and the sunlight,

00:22:52.890 --> 00:22:57.730
hashiru anata wo miteta

00:22:52.890 --> 00:22:57.730
I followed you running with my eyes.

00:22:57.940 --> 00:22:59.400
yume wo

00:22:57.940 --> 00:23:02.570
You were chasing your dream.

00:23:00.270 --> 00:23:02.570
oikaketeiru

00:23:02.570 --> 00:23:05.360
ground no ue ni

00:23:02.570 --> 00:23:08.570
Your sweat fell on the baseball field,

00:23:05.360 --> 00:23:08.570
ochiru ase ga

00:23:09.030 --> 00:23:12.540
mabushikatta yo

00:23:09.030 --> 00:23:12.540
and it looked so dazzling.

00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:19.960
wakariatteirutsumori datta

00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:19.960
I thought we understood each other,

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:27.260
issho ni warai naita kara

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:27.260
because you and I both shared laughs and tears.

00:23:27.930 --> 00:23:32.010
kokoro no ue ni

00:23:27.930 --> 00:23:35.030
There are identical footprints on both of our hearts.

00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:35.030
onaji ashi ato

00:23:35.030 --> 00:23:37.640
zutto mae kara

00:23:35.030 --> 00:23:42.690
I had unconciously liked you for a long while now.

00:23:37.640 --> 00:23:39.400
kizukazu ni

00:23:39.400 --> 00:23:42.690
suki ni natta

00:23:42.690 --> 00:23:44.980
atsuku sugoshita

00:23:42.690 --> 00:23:49.820
My feelings were hiding in the days we spent, full of passion.

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:49.820
tsukihi ni kakureteta

00:23:49.820 --> 00:23:52.410
zutto mae kara

00:23:49.820 --> 00:23:57.500
We've been drawn to each other for so long now.

00:23:52.410 --> 00:23:54.290
otagai ni

00:23:54.290 --> 00:23:57.500
hikareteita

00:23:57.500 --> 00:23:59.710
kono kimochi wa

00:23:57.500 --> 00:24:06.710
This feeling I have for you is what youth left behind.

00:23:59.710 --> 00:24:06.710
seishun no wasuremono

00:24:09.460 --> 00:24:14.820
Preview

00:24:09.460 --> 00:24:14.820
Preview

00:24:11.090 --> 00:24:15.580
I've been asked to be the closer in Watts' place for the final games,

00:24:15.580 --> 00:24:18.750
but my left arm's starting to feel worse and worse.

00:24:18.750 --> 00:24:20.100
What in the world's going on?

00:24:20.930 --> 00:24:23.790
Next time, on Major: The Dream Before Us.

00:24:24.480 --> 00:24:26.650
Run toward the stage of your dreams!

00:24:24.480 --> 00:24:30.160
Next Time

00:24:24.480 --> 00:24:30.160
Next Time

00:24:24.480 --> 00:24:30.160
The Dream Before Us

00:24:24.480 --> 00:24:30.160
The Dream Before Us
